# Commit names

When creating a git commit, write the subject as:

`action scope: description`

- **action:** a lowercase verb (`add`, `update`, `fix`, `accept`)
- **scope:** what was touched (phase, skill, rule, doc), in ordinary words
- **description:** after the colon, why, in a few words

Do not title-case the action. Do not omit the colon.
